    listening: [{ id: 'l1', lang: 'en-US', title: 'Not given or false?', text: 'Let me show you the trap. The text says that the museum was extended in two thousand and ten. The statement says that the museum was extended because visitor numbers had grown. Is that true? No. Is it false? Not really either. The text gives the year but says nothing about the reason. So the correct answer is not given. Students often choose false because the statement feels wrong, but false requires a contradiction, and here there is none.',
      qs: [{ q: 'What does the text say about the museum?', o: ['It was extended in 2010', 'It was closed in 2010', 'It was built in 1910', 'It was sold'], a: 0, kind: 'explicit' }, { q: 'Why is the answer «not given»?', o: ['The reason for the extension is not mentioned', 'The year is wrong', 'The museum is closed', 'The text is too long'], a: 0, kind: 'explicit' }, { q: 'What does «false» require, according to the speaker?', o: ['A contradiction with the text', 'A feeling that it is wrong', 'A different date', 'A long explanation'], a: 0, kind: 'implicit' }] }],
